Claude Opus 5.5 on 2026-11-18 at ~01:38:
The index is rebuilt from the three sketches, as you described, and it runs from disk (`index/index.html`). I tested it in headless Chrome at 1024×768, 1440×900 and 390×844.

**What I decided where your notes left room:**
- **Lattice:** 26 heads (14 on phones), slower and fainter than in the sketch. I also fixed a bug inherited from the sketch: heads could only enter near the screen corners. Now they come from anywhere along the edges. In the landscape layouts each link now gets about one strike every two seconds.
- **Nodes:** each node is a hexagon on the lattice, 12 steps from the centre. Hover or keyboard focus grows it in two steps to the larger hexagon with the big icon. On touch screens, the first tap opens a node and the second follows the link.
- **penquire:** both icons are built from your own strokes in Variable Compleja I:
  - The `e` and the `i` come from `e^{iθ} = cos θ + i sin θ` (p. 9), and the `+` from the same line.
  - The `π` comes from `e^{2πi}` (p. 11), with its bar cut short so it fits where θ stood.
  - The `1` comes from `e⁰ = 1` (p. 11).
  - The crossed 0 is the 0 from `z ≠ 0` (p. 9) with the slash from `|w|/|z|` laid over it.
  - They stay as images of the ink, like the formulas, because vectorising broke the pencil-like strokes.
- **CB Teo:** the big icon is the club's logo with its white turned to ink (the logo is white on a clear background). You didn't name a small icon, so I used the rack of its ten coloured ball-heads.
- **cv:** I drew a certificate with a gold seal, as you asked. If you want something less academic, a plain sheet of paper fits a CV better than a diploma or a mortarboard, and doesn't point at academia.
- **The other icons:** the treble clef is from the Noto Music font, whose licence allows this. The LitS figure is reduced to the circle, the gold arc, the dashed tangents, and the points p and q.
- **Headlines:** they sit under your name, one letter per lattice cell, and wrap onto a second line when they don't fit. When a head strikes one, the word opens out from that cell: a gold flash, a flicker of code, then the letter. It stays about 2 s, fades, and the next headline is placed hidden.
- **Ticker:** the quote and "BERTRAND RUSSELL" scroll hidden through a strip of up to 26 cells at the bottom left. A strike lights the strip for about 4.5 s; after it fades, it can't be struck again for 4–10 s. You only ever catch fragments.
- **Formulas:** they are hidden in two slots (top right, and to the left of the hexagon) and are revealed the same way as the words. Their placement and the mechanism are my choice, so say if you want them handled differently.
- **Links:** a head that hits a link is absorbed and sends a pulse both ways. When it reaches the node, firecoat glows (the drop-shadow glow from the orrery) and the other nodes' borders flash gold briefly. When it reaches the signet, it bumps that link's ring.
- **Signet:** the armillary's metal rings and faceted bb, cut to three bands, one per axis. A pulse from one link of a pair tips its band across the axis; one from the opposite link spins it about the axis. Bump size adjusts itself to how often pulses arrive, so the bands keep a gentle average speed on any screen. The signet starts whole and comes apart with the first pulses. Nothing pulls it back together.
- **Removed:** the top-right readout, the fixed points, both description texts, the quote block, and everything from the armillary scene you listed.
- **Node labels:** I kept only the names. The sketches' data lines and short descriptions were stand-ins written by Fable, so I dropped them; say if you want any back.

**Repo changes:**
- Iteration 31's milestone is in `milestones.md`, linking to its three gallery shots: `gallery/iteration031S1.png` (armillary), `S2.png` (lattice) and `S3.png` (orrery). Each was taken after its animations had played out.
- I added one sentence to CLAUDE.md's Gallery section, since that section asked for the capture rule to be recorded: shots are taken when the dynamic elements show.
- I'll take iteration 32's shot when you wrap up. The sketch folders and `design-brief.md` are untouched.
- The three.js library file (742 KB) is copied into `index/assets/` as it was in the sketches; it could be slimmed later.

**Decisions for you:**
- Certificate or plain sheet for the cv node.
- Whether the formulas stay where they are and appear this way.
- Whether the rings should slowly settle back into the signet when no pulses arrive.


Jonatan on 2026-11-18 at ~01:55:
This is looking great already. Please count this current form as an iteration. Some follow-ups for the next one:
- Node growth should not be done in two steps, but smoothly. I get why the decision, but it feels clunky.
- When a node opens, keeping the cursor right at the edge of the hexagon keeps the node open, which is correct. But the node does not open until the cursor gets into the closed node (or touches the title), which is a relatively small area. Instead, please make it so when the cursor gets within two levels of the closed node, it starts to open. If the cursor slowly approaches the first level, the node should slowly open towards the first level, so that both meet there. If the cursor gets to the first level then the cursor should open entirely. To keep smoothness, cap the velocity at which the node opens or closes.
- Please remove the sketch folders, we'll take it from here.
- Export what you deem appropriate from the design brief into the README, and remove the brief afterwards. Do not add bloat to the README. It should serve a human looking to get a hold of the repo and the website. We humans walk away the moment we feel our time is being wasted with minor detail when we are trying to understand something.
- Please start a terminology document in the root of the repo. Look into 1g49's policy for the same document and import it into this project. 'node', 'head', 'stream', 'signet', 'bb form', 'db form'.
- We are going to be updating the cv site in one of the next sessions. When we do, the iteration that happens, the gallery shot should be from the cv site. Assuming this index page has not has substantial modifications. In general, the gallery shot/s shuold account for the non-trivial changes that took place in that iteration. For instance, if one iteration modifies the pdf cv, cv site, and index page, then a shot should be taken from all those three.
- Please get rid of the writing effect that makes the equations appear. When two heads collide, an outwards wave effect in the region the equation image occupies, and the equation should emerge as in a pulse, like the pulse on the links to the nodes. Color should be that same gold. The wave should only clear the streams on that area momentarily for the equation to emerge but, right after that, the streams that happen to cross the image should be visible underneath it (so equation images should be transparent where there's no ink; this will look a bit rough until we work on penquire a bit more, but that's alright).
- There are too few equations, so they start repeating after just a little while. Please go gather more equations, from various areas. Unless you're saving the equations in equations.js like you are due to speed concerns, please start a folder in assets to host them.
- Equations should not emerge even if two heads collide if there's not room to show them in allowed areas; anything outside the signet and opened nodes, my name, the cryptic phrases (gotta find a better name for that!), and other equations. And let's require that no more than two equations are active at the same time (heads colliding when a new equation doesn't have room should not trigger a wave).
- Make the first letter of my surnames the same color as the heads, and the cryptic phrases too.
- I think I have a much better way to share Russell's quote: put it into a head! I'll let you decide on the details and polish this if I deem it necessary.
- I've done a bit of research on the shoulders-of-giants quote. I have a very personal understanding of it that fits firecoat.me rather than this website, but I now know that the usual meaning people give it is one tightly tied to scientific advance. That also makes sense, and I have no problem overloading the definition in my head. So let's make Newton's quote (even though the quote predates him) another easter egg by giving him a head too.
- And a final easter egg would be one that winks at firecoat.me. Won't enter into the details, but it should read '∃·1△@𝄞 —there exist something truly mesmerizing about fire'.
- The Teo small logo should be the crossed 8 ball from 1g49's assets/teo_wordmark.svg. Notice that it is a very simple logo: 'TE' followed by an annular section with an '8' and a oblique rectangle, without a white circle about the 8, and then 'CLUB BILLAR' on the right. This svg needs redoing because the countours are rough wherever they don't align with the x or y directions. You got potrace installed so you should be able to get a clean replacement. Once you're done with it, remove the current one with the new, and import the crossed 8 ball representation (the logo without 'TE' and 'CLUB BILLAR') as the small icon. Commit the replacement in 1g49 with a minimal message.
- The lattice should be just a bit less subtle. I can see the slightly bigger dots in a triangulation of it. It's a nice touch, so make those also less subtle. Also, put an even bigger one where the links from the nodes converge. That should land exactly between the two b's. That small region could become too hard too crowded, so maybe enlarge the whole signet around 10% in radius.
- The links that join the nodes to the signet should go all the way to the center/origin dot (the one the previous point introduces). And they should be black. Make the black hexagons that enclose the nodes just a tad thicker, and the links towards the center dot the same thickness and color. Also, extend the links past the nodes 3 levels, without being visible on the inside of the nodes of course. These 3-level extensions should end with an arrow shape. Not a regular arrow: take the db logo and shift the 'd' to the right until it touches the 'b'; the resulting arrow made by the tips would be it.
- Please replace my name's fonts with the same that are used for the streams.
- Please make the center dot act as a dynamo for the movement of the rings: when a head collides with a link or node enclosing, a pulse should propagate through it until the center dot, which should be illuminated and move the ring in the direction of its connection accordingly.
- Notice that the links and node contours should be "the same material than the signet", meaning the lighting should be a similar effect.
- When a pulse gets to an arrow, it should have a 50% chance of emmiting a head.
- Yes, please make the rings slowly settle back into the signet's initial state when no pulses arrive. That's a nice touch!
We are going to end the session next turn, because this is getting too thick, so please propose commits at the end of your response. We'll address your follow-ups and continue in the next session. Try your best please!

